From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: JitArm64: two upstream changes after e6583f8

- Conditional branches stay in near code (dolphin-emu PR #12319, JosJuice):
  a taken bcx/bclrx no longer jumps into far code and back, which every
  loop back-edge is.
- dcbz_l uses the JIT's dcbz instead of the interpreter (from PR #13929,
  Martino Fontana): both clear a line through ClearDCacheLine, and the
  locked cache at 0xE0000000 is mapped like RAM; only the HID checks, which
  the JIT's dcbz does not do either, differ. The SDK's LCEnable runs it in
  a loop.

On an RG52 Mini, the ND Demo, frames 300-2400, three runs each, built
alike: 45.33, 45.28, 44.81 fps before; 47.30, 47.36, 47.20 with the first
(+4.8%); 46.84, 47.12, 47.36 with both (the demo seldom runs dcbz_l).

